From 5ea8d51ff6c6eea58f9f3ab720e8f4c499e02abb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 13:20:24 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] VideoOutput: the stereo layer takes a plain 3D video from the
 decoder's textures

The layer's presenter drew the views of a frame into the compositor's window surface
only for the drawn views of a depth video (layerSourceOf). Every other 3D video, a
plain full side by side file included, was read back from the GPU, converted on the
processor and copied into wl_shm buffers: about 250 to 280 percent of one core for a
3840x1080 clip at 30 frames a second, on AMD and on NVIDIA, with the decoder's frames
already on the GPU.

PlainUnpacker takes the views of a decoder frame apart where they are. The frame is
imported as the depth route imports it (QHwVideoBuffer::mapTextures through a QRhi on
the drawing context: VA-API and CUDA), and one pass for each view converts the planes
to RGB at the content's depth (RGBA8, or RGBA16 above 8 bits) into one texture, the
first view of the packing at the left, each view at the size its samples have: a
rectangle of the frame (side by side, top and bottom), every second row, every second
column, the row's own checkers (H.264 Table D-8, H.265 Table D.8, Matroska StereoMode,
RFC 9559), or the frame of each eye of a frame sequence. Nothing is interpolated or
resized. The presenter hands that texture to the layer as it does the drawn views, so
the layer draws it into its window surface with the crop and the eye order.

The drawing context asks EGL for no reset notification: the layer's own context shares it, and EGL
refuses a share list of contexts with different notification strategies (Mesa: "share list notification
strategy mismatch", EGL_BAD_MATCH, on radeonsi, llvmpipe and NVIDIA alike), which the first run of the
GPU route on the installed package showed as the layer falling back to wl_shm.

A frame the GPU cannot take apart (decoded by the processor, a pixel format the passes
do not read, a converter that refuses the DMA-BUF) still goes through wl_shm, and the
presenter's log says why; a multiview stream keeps the copy. A log line says when the
GPU route is on. A layer that refuses the views of a depth (NVIDIA 615 has no 16 bit unsigned window
surface, and the compositor lists no XB48 modifier) is asked again every sixtieth frame, and the frames
in between are copied at once with the reason, so the GPU does not take apart what the layer will not draw.

tst_qquickvideostereo::plainPackingsOnTheGpu: every packing at 8, 10, 12 and 16 bit
words, the views predicted from the packing alone, no read back, the textures mapped
once for a frame and twice for a frame sequence. plainFramesTheGpuCannotTake: the
refusals are said. plainViewsAreSharedByTheLayersContext: the layer's kind of context can share the unpacker's
(red: EGL error 0x3009).

Upstream: Qt has no compositor layer; dev (searched 2026-11-10) only reshapes
QHwVideoBuffer (mapTextures overloads, HandleType deprecated).

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 via Claude Code
